Section name: Related Work
Excerpt:
Language models have gained popularity due to their proficiency at comprehending human lan- guage. Nevertheless, prior research has examined numerous limitations of these models, particularly in terms of their reliability and fairness. Various techniques have been previously presented to miti- gate bias in language models while enhancing their reliability. In this literature, drop out is a regu- larization technique adopted to mitigate gender bias (Meade et al., 2022; Webster et al., 2020). The interruption generated by this strategy restricts the model from acquiring the ability to detect the connections between words that ultimately builds stereotypes. Some studies propose reducing bias in pre-trained models and enhancing dependabil- ity through diverse data augmentation. This in- volves incorporating data points that cover various demographics (Zmigrod et al., 2019; Dinan et al., 2020

Section name: Benefits
Excerpt:
